  For even in the gentlest stream,
  Flows the heart of nature's dream.

  In the river's endless journey,
  We might see our own refrain,
  Moving onward, always forward,
  Through the sunshine and the rain,
  Carving paths we've never traced,
  Finding beauty in our pace.

